  "preamble": "Prothesis of a velar nasal [ŋ] before an initial vowel. In Samoyedic, Nganasan and Tundra Nenets added ŋ- to words that began with a vowel in Proto-Samoyedic (Nganasan ӈамтә 'antler' < *amtə, Tundra Nenets ӈоба 'glove' < *opå). In Hong Kong Cantonese, the merger of /ŋ/ with the null initial has produced hypercorrect ŋ- in words with a historical null initial, as in 愛 oi3 'love' pronounced ngoi3.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Prothesis, Epenthesis, Hypercorrection",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Nganasan",
      "languageFamily": "Samoyedic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *amtə 'horn, antler'",
          "to": "ӈамтә ŋamtə",
          "note": "Prothetic ŋ- before initial *a; Tundra Nenets has palatalized n- (нямд)."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *aŋ 'mouth'",
          "to": "ӈаӈ ŋaŋ",
          "note": "Northern Selkup ө̄ӈ, without prothesis."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *opå 'glove'",
          "to": "ӈуху ŋuhu"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Tundra Nenets",
      "languageFamily": "Samoyedic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *opå 'glove'",
          "to": "ӈоба ŋoba",
          "note": "Forest Nenets ӈопа; Forest Enets оба without prothesis."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *op 'one'",
          "to": "ӈобˮ"
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Samoyedic *åj 'foot'",
          "to": "ӈэ"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Hong Kong Cantonese",
      "languageFamily": "Yue",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "愛 oi3 /ɔːi/ 'love'",
          "to": "ngoi3 /ŋɔːi/",
          "note": "Hypercorrection by speakers who restore the /ŋ/ lost in the 'lazy sound' merger of /ŋ/ with the null initial, extending it to words that never had it."
        },
        {
          "from": "屋 [ʊk] 'house'",
          "to": "[ŋʊk]"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
